Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Categorization of Possible Solutions for the Linear Problem", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.748780318182393*^9, 
  3.7487803730728817`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0a72ecbc-d563-48da-baf5-\
5729a0349c28"],

Cell["\<\
Speculate on a description for each possible category for different linear \
problems corresponding to different eigenvalues. Note, for a matrix with real \
coefficients, complex eigenvalues must appear as a complex conjugate pair. \
What is the implication of this when you only have 3 independent variables?\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.748780391452719*^9, 
  3.7487805098355565`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a18fc849-b79a-4500-bd1f-\
b4da50fccf58"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" The Nonlinear Problem", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.748780318182393*^9, 3.7487803730728817`*^9}, {
  3.7488791493190985`*^9, 
  3.748879178071974*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"90c241a4-63fd-41c7-956f-\
5c99bad64bf4"],

Cell["Consider the linear problem displayed above:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7488792067178383`*^9, 
  3.748879225946761*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0e3b37d0-2796-4ba7-a332-\
755a0a45e172"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
  RowBox[{"u1", ",", "u2", ",", "u3"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1115]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1426e0ac-eaa1-4fb3-9303-6da3d7441faf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It exhibits some of the basic behavior of a tornado in this basic linear \
form.\n\nModify the linear right-hand side ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
    RowBox[{"u1", ",", "u2", ",", "u3"}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "d1f6f924-697b-4732-9575-3c090b810bef"],
 " with a nonlinear replacement to create a new vector field (the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]-\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote] sign is to cause the vector \
field to rotate counterclockwise and increase upward as well)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7488792883409996`*^9, 3.748879403338498*^9}, {
  3.7488811451796646`*^9, 
  3.748881168593006*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"248658e1-668c-4579-8cc8-\
45973a7b13d2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"VectorPlot3D", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "u1"}], "+", 
        RowBox[{"3", " ", "u2"}]}], 
       RowBox[{"1", "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
         FractionBox[
          SuperscriptBox[
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               SuperscriptBox["u1", "2"], "+", 
               SuperscriptBox["u2", "2"]}], ")"}], "-", "1", "-", 
             RowBox[{
              SuperscriptBox["u3", "2"], "/", "8"}]}], ")"}], "2"], "10"]]}]],
       ",", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "3"}], " ", "u1"}], 
       RowBox[{"1", "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
         FractionBox[
          SuperscriptBox[
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               SuperscriptBox["u1", "2"], "+", 
               SuperscriptBox["u2", "2"]}], ")"}], "-", "1", "-", 
             RowBox[{
              SuperscriptBox["u3", "2"], "/", "8"}]}], ")"}], "2"], "10"]]}]],
       ",", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"-", "u3"}], 
       RowBox[{"20", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", "+", 
          SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
           FractionBox[
            SuperscriptBox[
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                 SuperscriptBox["u1", "2"], "+", 
                 SuperscriptBox["u2", "2"]}], ")"}], "-", "1", "-", 
               RowBox[{
                SuperscriptBox["u3", "2"], "/", "8"}]}], ")"}], "2"], 
            "10"]]}], ")"}]}]]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"u1", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", "5"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"u2", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", "5"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"u3", ",", "0", ",", "10"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"Axes", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<u1\>\"", ",", "\"\<u2\>\"", ",", "\"\<u3\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
   ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"BoxRatios", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1.5"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"VectorPoints", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"20", ",", "20", ",", "6"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"VectorScale", "\[Rule]", ".1"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7487807896145315`*^9, 3.7487808349350634`*^9}, {
   3.7487808655921288`*^9, 3.7487809509096594`*^9}, 3.748780986895258*^9, {
   3.748781029441512*^9, 3.7487811444310093`*^9}, {3.748781182759842*^9, 
   3.7487812772442894`*^9}, {3.74878134615518*^9, 3.748781383098874*^9}, 
   3.7487814498025436`*^9, {3.7487814812196856`*^9, 3.7487814943159943`*^9}, 
   3.7487815523517976`*^9, {3.7487816693604975`*^9, 3.7487816970472655`*^9}, {
   3.7487817372582865`*^9, 3.7487817583373938`*^9}, {3.7487817911886787`*^9, 
   3.748781793162876*^9}, {3.7488671860136676`*^9, 3.7488672340218663`*^9}, {
   3.748867264034865*^9, 3.7488673096733007`*^9}, {3.748867564663769*^9, 
   3.748867627008769*^9}, {3.7488677513947687`*^9, 3.7488678045357685`*^9}, {
   3.7488678596847687`*^9, 3.7488679928967686`*^9}, {3.7488680297757688`*^9, 
   3.7488680439737687`*^9}, {3.748868077732769*^9, 3.748868124968769*^9}, {
   3.748868165023769*^9, 3.748868222991769*^9}, {3.748868328395115*^9, 
   3.748868362504525*^9}, {3.7488683983921137`*^9, 3.748868431408415*^9}, {
   3.7488750613063383`*^9, 3.7488750922194295`*^9}, {3.748875145690776*^9, 
   3.7488751930455112`*^9}, {3.748875227359942*^9, 3.748875291018307*^9}, {
   3.748875348769082*^9, 3.748875378144019*^9}, 3.7488754718863926`*^9, {
   3.7488755139005933`*^9, 3.7488755844296455`*^9}, {3.748875619665169*^9, 
   3.7488756240036025`*^9}, 3.748875690906292*^9, {3.748875848043004*^9, 
   3.748875848954095*^9}, {3.7488759442076197`*^9, 3.7488759449986987`*^9}, 
   3.7488759753047295`*^9, {3.7488761254027376`*^9, 3.74887613263346*^9}, {
   3.748876165820779*^9, 3.7488761691871157`*^9}, {3.7488763065188475`*^9, 
   3.7488764648836823`*^9}, 3.748876501039297*^9, {3.748876569200113*^9, 
   3.7488765716893616`*^9}, {3.74887943666183*^9, 3.7488794703541994`*^9}, 
   3.748879851782338*^9},ExpressionUUID->"6969a631-2f7d-4b80-a51a-\
7a9051192bbe"],

Cell["\<\
The new vector field displayed with 6 horizontal slices illustrates a \
possible velocity vector field for a tornado. Tilt the above plot several \
different ways to get a better feeling for the calculation. Observe that the \
nonlinear modification is from one of the VERY limited number of possible \
linear configurations that exist in three dimensions for a first-order \
system. In fact, all possible linear combinations with real eigenvalues are \
inconsistent with the velocity profile generated within a tornado (as they \
will not rotate). Also, if there is one complex valued eigenvalue, then it \
must exist as a complex valued pair with the third eigenvalue being real. \
This is the ONLY possible linear configuration that will yield a circular \
pattern in 3 dimensional space from a first-order system. Is it any wonder \
that a tornado in 3 dimensional space absolutely must look something like it \
does with a rotating pattern parallel to the ground and a rising simple \
vertical shape? On the other hand, if the physics dictates that the governing \
equations are second, third or even fourth order differential equations in 3 \
dimensional space, then many other patterns are possible. But once again, the \
list of possible patterns will be highly restricted. Most of these patterns \
can be excluded immediately because they are incompatible with the \
fundamental rotational nature of a tornado, leaving even fewer possibilities \
for a model. Finally, if all possible patterns are excluded as being \
incompatible with the fundamental behavior of a tornado, then ALL possible \
models using this procedure will be guaranteed to fail.

As a side note, this was always the dream in the development of string \
theory. If all quantum particles could be described as different modes of \
vibration (including harmonics) of a one-dimensional string or a \
multidimensional membrane in a higher dimensional space, then there would \
only be a limited number of possible vibrational patterns. Wouldn\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t it be glorious if there was one and only one vibrational \
pattern that can create the particles that we observe in our universe? Then, \
if the universe is constructed according to string theory, it is the way it \
is because it is the only way that it can be. Sadly, this dream has been \
crushed as subsequent work has shown an ever increasing number of possible \
configurations consistent with our observations. As a consequence, string \
theory has been largely relegated to one of the many dead end journeys that \
physics often takes in the search for truth.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7488794905482187`*^9, 3.748879613955558*^9}, {
   3.7488797018383455`*^9, 3.748879745828744*^9}, 3.748879777964957*^9, {
   3.748879875134673*^9, 3.748879875313691*^9}, {3.748879917048864*^9, 
   3.748880106205778*^9}, {3.748880151242281*^9, 3.7488802012522817`*^9}, {
   3.748880251910347*^9, 3.748880325406696*^9}, {3.748880383276482*^9, 
   3.7488803910522594`*^9}, {3.7488804332574797`*^9, 
   3.7488804496451187`*^9}, {3.7488804807472286`*^9, 
   3.7488809264427934`*^9}, {3.7488810377759256`*^9, 3.74888104712186*^9}, {
   3.748881313724518*^9, 3.7488813575769024`*^9}, {3.7488814069828424`*^9, 
   3.748881513449488*^9}, {3.7488815764197845`*^9, 
   3.7488815764657893`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4cc45063-7bf0-4f62-a32a-\
306d456dd194"]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]]
},
